# Line endings.
#
# Everything is stored as LF and checked out as LF, on every platform, whatever
# the local git configuration says.
#
# This matters on Windows, where git's system configuration sets
# core.autocrlf=true: a checkout then rewrites every text file to CRLF, and
# `gofmt -l` reports the entire source tree as unformatted. The Linux job checks
# out LF and stays green, so without this the difference only appears in the
# Windows job and at release time.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch scripts keep CRLF; cmd.exe is most predictable with it.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
